cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below, together with ANKYRA (listed under references)."
type: software
title: "Building_load_ANKYRA_lite (ankyra-lite): month-ahead hourly load forecasting with a small self-developed carrier network and the ANKYRA anchoring layer"
abstract: >-
  ankyra-lite is a self-contained month-ahead (744-hour) hourly load forecaster for buildings, industrial meters and
  households that needs no foundation model. A small self-developed carrier network (a copy-pointer structured load
  network with 61,613 parameters, trained from scratch per population) forecasts the month after a forecast origin
  from the unit's own history and the known calendar. Its forecasts at the origin and at up to six earlier
  pseudo-origins are passed to an unchanged copy of the ANKYRA 2.2.1 anchoring layer, which estimates per-unit
  combination weights from the unit's own completed pseudo-forecasts and returns the hourly trajectory, the month's
  energy and the monthly peak readout. The repository contains the package, its training recipe, equivalence tests
  against the research code and the original ANKYRA package, the evaluation code, and a re-evaluation against 21
  baselines (22 forecasters) on nine populations (hourly, energy, peak, conventional metrics, forecast-day,
  error-block, scaled-error and rank-test tables).
